s to a significant reduction in glomerular filtration rate, impairing the kidneys' ability to excrete metabolic waste and maintain fluid and electrolyte balance. Acute renal failure often occurs as a complication of various medical conditions, including severe rhabdomyolysis, which may be linked to the use of statins.\n\nPatients experiencing acute renal failure, particularly those in intensive care, have specific nutritional needs that must be addressed to manage their condition effectively. These needs include adjustments in dietary protein and energy intake, tailored to the patient's overall health status and the type of treatment being administered. The management of acute renal failure requires adherence to specific nutritional guidelines to prevent complications and support recovery, especially in critically ill patients who may experience severe hypercatabolism.\n\nIn summary, \"\"INSUFICIENCIA RENAL AGUDA\"\" is a serious condition that necessitates immediate medical intervention and careful nutritional management to mitigate its effects on the body and promote recovery.\",28\r\n2200,DIÁLISIS PERITONEAL,\"DIÁLISIS PERITONEAL is a type of dialysis that utilizes the lining of the abdomen to filter waste from the blood, serving as an alternative to hemodialysis for patients with renal failure. This treatment method is specifically designed for individuals with chronic kidney disease, allowing for the removal of bodily waste. It is important to note that peritoneal dialysis requires patients to increase their caloric intake due to the presence of glucose in the dialysis fluid. Overall, DIÁLISIS PERITONEAL provides a viable option for those suffering from kidney insufficiency, leveraging the body's own abdominal lining to facilitate the filtration process.\",6\r\n2191,HEMODIÁLISIS,\"Hemodialysis is a medical procedure designed to filter waste products and excess fluid from the blood in patients whose kidneys are not functioning properly. This treatment is essential for individuals experiencing renal failure, whether acute or chronic, and is particularly important in advanced stages of chronic kidney disease. Hemodialysis requires central venous access and involves the use of a machine that performs the filtration process. \n\nIn addition to removing waste products, hemodialysis also helps to eliminate excess phosphorus from the blood, which is crucial for managing the health of patients with renal failure. The procedure necessitates specific dietary adjustments and careful nutritional management to support the patient's overall health during treatment. \n\nHemodialysis is commonly employed in clinical settings, such as during a patient's stay in an intensive care unit (UCI), where it is vital for managing acute renal failure. Overall, hemodialysis serves as a critical intervention for patients with kidney dysfunction, ensuring the removal of harmful substances from the bloodstream and maintaining fluid balance.\",16\r\n4375,RABDOMIÓLISIS,\"Rabdomiólisis, also known as rhabdomyolysis, is a serious medical condition characterized by the breakdown of muscle tissue. This condition can complicate the management of diabetes and may arise as a severe side effect of statin medications, which are commonly prescribed to lower cholesterol levels. The breakdown of muscle tissue in rabdomiólisis can lead to significant health issues, including the risk of kidney failure.\",2\r\n10069,BICARBONATOS,,1\r\n11381,DIÁLISIS PERITONEAL CONTINUA,Continuous peritoneal dialysis is a treatment that allows for a lower risk of hyperkalemia due to constant therapy.,1\r\n2190,NUTRICIÓN EN LA UCI,,1\r\n2182,P. JUSTO PAVÍA,P. Justo Pavía is an author contributing to the chapter on nutrition in renal insufficiency.,1\r\n\n\n-----Relationships-----\nhuman_readable_id,source,target,description,combined_degree\r\n4756,NUTRICIÓN PARENTERAL,INSUFICIENCIA RENAL AGUDA,\"NUTRICIÓN PARENTERAL is a medical intervention that may be necessary for patients suffering f